# MiSTerEmby config — copy to /media/fat/misteremby/emby.conf and fill in.
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored. Setting names are not
# case-sensitive; values are used exactly as written.
#
# The only line you need is your Emby server's address (the same one you'd
# type into a browser; a trailing /emby or / is fine):

SERVER=http://192.168.2.10:8096

# With just that, MiSTerEmby shows an Emby Connect PIN on first launch. On
# any phone or computer go to https://emby.media/pin, sign in with your Emby
# Connect account, and type the PIN in. Your Emby user has to be linked to
# that Emby Connect account (Emby: Settings > Users > your user > Emby
# Connect). The sign-in is saved to token.conf next to this file, so it only
# has to be done once.

# TV mode — PAL or NTSC. Optional, defaults to PAL.
PAL


# ── Signing in with a password instead ─────────────────────────────────────
# For a local Emby user that isn't linked to Emby Connect. The password sits
# in this file in plain text — once the first sign-in has worked (token.conf
# exists) you can delete the PASSWORD= line and the saved sign-in keeps
# working.
#
# USERNAME=your-emby-username
# PASSWORD=your-emby-password


# ── Signing in with an Emby Connect account, no PIN ────────────────────────
# Same result as the PIN, without the trip to emby.media/pin. Same plain-text
# caveat as above.
#
# CONNECT_USER=you@example.com
# CONNECT_PASSWORD=your-emby-connect-password


# ── Using an API key instead ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Still supported. An API key is created in the Emby server dashboard under
# Advanced > API Keys (name it "MiSTerEmby" so it's recognisable later), and
# needs the username whose watch state it should update:
#
# API_KEY=your-api-key-here
# USERNAME=your-emby-username
#
# A PIN or password sign-in is preferable where you have the choice. An API
# key isn't scoped to a user: it authenticates as the server, and USERNAME
# only decides which account this client writes watch state to. The same key
# can read and write any account on the server — a much broader credential
# than the job needs — and creating one needs admin access.
#
# The older positional layout (server on line 1, API key on line 2,
# username on line 3) is still read too.


# ── Transcode profile ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional — "WxH" or "WxH@BITRATE", e.g. 480x270@8000000. It's what Emby is
# asked to scale video down to before mplayer scales it to fill the screen;
# the default is 720x576@12000000. The pause screen shows which profile is
# actually in effect. Lower it if a weak network makes playback stutter.
#
# 480x270@8000000


# ── Cinema Mode ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Add a line containing just CINEMA_MODE to play trailers before a film you
# start from the beginning, like Emby's own apps do. Which trailers (and any
# custom intros) is decided by the Emby server's Cinema Mode settings. UP
# skips a trailer; A stops.
#
# CINEMA_MODE


# ── Direct streaming ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SD files in a codec the MiSTer decodes easily (DivX/Xvid MPEG-4, MPEG-1,
# progressive MPEG-2) are streamed with their video untouched: Emby only
# repackages it and converts the audio, which takes almost no work on a
# server without hardware transcoding. HD, H.264/HEVC and interlaced DVD
# sources are always transcoded. Add a line containing just
# TRANSCODE_ALWAYS to transcode everything instead, e.g. if a direct-streamed
# file plays badly.
#
# TRANSCODE_ALWAYS


# ── Troubleshooting: request log ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Add a line containing just DEBUGLOG and MiSTerEmby writes
# /media/fat/misteremby/debug.log. Off by default; the file is overwritten
# fresh on every launch, so it only ever holds one session's worth.
#
# One line per server request (method, endpoint, ok/FAIL, how long it took,
# how many bytes came back), plus a handful of one-shot lines at startup and
# during playback: framebuffer geometry, which input devices were found,
# the relevant MiSTer.ini display settings (ypbpr/scandoubler/video_mode/...
# — see docs/DISPLAY_COMPATIBILITY.md), which menu core/DDR path is active,
# the GitHub update check result, and the transcode profile/resolution each
# time something plays.
#
# It does NOT log your server address, API key, access token, password, PIN,
# anything from a request's query string, user or item ids, or what's
# actually in your library (no titles) — safe to attach debug.log to a
# GitHub issue as-is.
#
# DEBUGLOG


# ── HTTPS with a self-signed certificate ───────────────────────────────────
# MiSTerEmby verifies your server's TLS certificate by default. If your Emby
# server is https:// with a self-signed certificate, that verification will
# fail — add a line containing just INSECURE_TLS to skip it. Only needed for
# https with a self-signed cert; a plain http:// server (the usual setup)
# doesn't use TLS at all and ignores this. Emby Connect itself
# (connect.emby.media) is always verified.
#
# INSECURE_TLS
